^"stream"{
 >>[2026-10-13 22:10] observe — the creator asked for a plan to revise brace semantics while asking for a `< & >` hero on spw.quest (handles that answer tap, swipe and drag; ghost boxes that take `.` or `~`; `{` labeled into `{_paper`), a runtime improved "this way", a home door into spw.quest from the cauldron, clipboard or pins, and a rethink of page, region and component serialization, noting that expressions reached elements through copy units before there was granular enhancement or edge preweighting.
 >>[2026-10-13 22:20] verify — two read-only surveys. Braces: each pair has four to six meanings across WB canon, the site registry, the conventions and WB theory; `{ }` is definition in canon and direction in the registry. The parser sets no label: `{_paper a }_paper` reads `_paper` as words and reports success; the AST's openLabel and closeLabel fields are never set. Serialization: eleven serializers, eleven shapes; the cauldron writes fallback words onto data-spw-semantic-expression; pins keep no expression; nothing reads the clipboard; the kin index is built in the page on every load.
 >>[2026-10-13 22:30] decide — plan written, nothing built. Five decisions go to the creator before any slice that depends on what a pair means; slices 2 and 3 wait on nothing.
 >>[2026-10-27 13:40] hygiene — decision 1 moves from ^"open" into index.spw as #>wonder_brace_semantics_curly_name, with an answer set and a probe; decisions 2 to 5 stay plain questions until 1 is answered.
 >>[2026-10-27 13:40] probe — wonder_brace_semantics_curly_name: the probe counts each word in any role, so it is noisy. The registry's six definition hits are a variable (OPERATOR_DEFINITIONS.map((definition) …)); as the pair's name it says direction only, as expected. The conventions say behavior 27 times and direction 9; definition appears as a field key and as the brace's original meaning (operator-semantics.spw:317), not as a workbench quote, so that half of the ~#expect missed.
 >>[2026-11-05 23:45] cache — the creator recalled three early readings (a highlighter color per container across a paragraph, "of" as a concept in {chronicles} <of> (narnia), <&> as a typed placeholder) and asked whether they were better than what replaced them or whether drift needs revisiting. Held as #>wonder_brace_semantics_highlighter_then_now, then and now side by side, no verdict. The same day the creator decided that each brace pair names its slot wherever it sits, which both readings need.
 >>[2026-11-06 11:30] plan — a session drafted Slice 3.5 (the element pair in @block_association), a two-way contract for Spw-native hosts with four archetypes, and edits to @serialization_hydration; left uncommitted, reviewed below.
 >>[2026-11-06 12:10] probe — the element pair, through both readers: serializeElementToSpw's #>card_one[topic[lens]{a, b}] parses in @workbench_reader with 0 errors and 0 warnings (the line reads as the handle's mode), and parseSpwDefinition reads subject "" and mode "topic[lens", so the draft's "fails to parse" was wrong and "loses the word" is right. The draft's two-line fix fails too: expressionLineFrom takes "#>card_one" as the expression. One line, #>card_one topic[lens]{a, b}(studio)<receipt>, keeps every slot through readExpressionSlots in either order, and readSlotOrder keeps the author's. Neither function has a caller; parser.hydrate(el) already names the read in site.js.
 >>[2026-11-06 12:14] probe — the draft's host claims: the lens switch already writes its [seat] (@lens_modes writeLensModeState, line 357) and takes requests only through requestLensMode (lens:request), not spw:variant-selected; its seats are data-set-mode with aria-pressed, not data-mode with aria-controls. svg-tunability.js writes no expression and round-trips its tuning as URL params. "silent seat" lives on /design/components/#lens-seat-b.
 >>[2026-11-06 12:16] probe — wonder_brace_semantics_highlighter_then_now: 1086 lines in *.html carry data-spw-semantic-expression (1089 attributes), against 1,075 hosts on 2026-10-13; the ~#expect held.
 >>[2026-11-06 12:18] probe — wonder_brace_semantics_curly_name, again: @operator_registry's header now sets its word beside the workbench's (lines 23-24, f66451dc: { } direction "where the workbench says … definition"), so the registry reads direction as its mutation of definition. Counts: registry definition 7 and direction 7 (definition is that header and a variable), operator-semantics.spw behavior 14, direction 8, definition 5, semantic-braces.spw behavior 13.
 >>[2026-11-06 12:20] probe — wonder_brace_semantics_first_way_back: writes at lens-modes.js:357, experiments.js:682 and :706, boonhonk-mixer.js:356, :524 and :526, and no readExpressionSlots in any of them. The chip writes its line as text and a title (renderLiveExpression), not as an attribute, so that clause of the ~#expect missed.
 >>[2026-11-06 12:24] revise — draft kept: the element pair as an ungated slice (3.5), the one-line block, the hosts that write their line, the no-write-back rule. Cut: the archetype table's wrong attribute and event names, "expose readSpwHydration" (it exists), a write under the name hydrate, the proposed-commit facet. Slices 2 and 3 split into 2a/2b and 3a/3b; 3b found the boon and bane alias in layout.css, cinematic.css and four recipe routes, not only brace-pivots.js. Refs re-measured: core.css:1596, spw.d.ts:281, toSpwExpression, constructSpell, buildPinRecord, ensureElementDeepLink.
}

^"open"{
